From c2ce31f4ec3887554c32f6bb441320b335027927 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: m5agent <m5agent@m5stack.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 22:32:44 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] hw/m5stopwatch: align VMeter default ADS1115 config with its
 driver

The 0130 VMeter branch reused the AMeter default config (0x8b80: PGA_256,
gain 5) even though VoltmeterUnit never writes a gain in its constructor and
assumes PGA_2048 (gain 2) + RATE_128 in its own resolution table. The model's
inverse-derived conversion therefore disagreed with the guest's conversion
formula on the default path. Use the ADS1115 power-on-style config 0x8580
(OS ready, single-shot, RATE_128, gain 2) so the default path is
self-consistent. Explicit set_gain() writes remain honoured.

No other semantics changed; catalogue stays planned until guest evidence
passes.

(Rebased by patch-chain reconciliation: base is the canonical order batch-4 chain + 0130; applied before 0135/0132.)
---
 hw/m5stopwatch/m5_unit_i2c_sensors.c | 7 ++++++-
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/hw/m5stopwatch/m5_unit_i2c_sensors.c b/hw/m5stopwatch/m5_unit_i2c_sensors.c
index 54cec48..2533c4d 100644
--- a/hw/m5stopwatch/m5_unit_i2c_sensors.c
+++ b/hw/m5stopwatch/m5_unit_i2c_sensors.c
@@ -1756,7 +1756,12 @@ void m5_unit_sensor_realize(M5Unit *u, Error **errp)
          * the driver's 0.015918958 divider. The synthetic EEPROM record keeps
          * calibration factor 1.0; it is NOT a real factory calibration. */
         s->kind = US_ADS1115_VMETER; address = 0x49;
-        s->command = 0x8b80;
+        /* VMeter never writes a gain in its constructor and assumes PGA_2048
+         * (gain 2) + RATE_128 in single-shot mode. The 0130 branch inherited
+         * the AMeter default (gain 5), which disagreed with the driver's own
+         * resolution table and made the default read path inconsistent. Use
+         * the ADS1115 power-on-style config so both sides agree. */
+        s->command = 0x8580;
         add_number(s, "voltage-v", 0, 5.0, -36, 36, false);
         object_property_add(OBJECT(u), "adc-raw", "int", ameter_raw_get, NULL, NULL, s);
         object_property_add(OBJECT(u), "config-word", "int", ameter_config_get, NULL, NULL, s);
